Spec: ServiceInstance

Purpose:
  Carry the full cluster-side contract of one service-package installation: declare the install
    coordinate (`jukebox`, `category`, `package`, opaque `options`, optional `initFrom`
    restore request), track per-stage install progress and children/services inventory in
    @ServiceInstanceStatus through @ApplicationCondition records, serve a TTL-cached
    cluster-wide index of published service keys, and register @ServiceInstance with its full
    accessor and mutator bridge onto package @rhai::Engine instances.

Owns:
  ./instanceservice.rs

References:
  ./instance_macros.sdd — frozen contract of every macro-attached lookup, status patch, event
    publication, stage setter and Rhai bridge this file attaches and names in `Exposes`; their
    behaviour is owned there and not restated here.
  ./ttl_cache.sdd — freshness, coalescing and error-keeps-slot contract governing the cache
    inside @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names.

Must:
  The @kube::CustomResource derive over @ServiceInstanceSpec generates the @ServiceInstance
    resource kind `ServiceInstance` in group `vynil.solidite.fr`, version `v1`, namespaced
    scope, shortname `vsvc`, plural `serviceinstances`, with status type @ServiceInstanceStatus
    and CRD doc `Custom resource representing an Vynil service package installation`.
  The CRD printer columns are, in order and by `jsonPath`: `Juke` -> `.spec.jukebox`,
    `cat` -> `.spec.category`, `pkg` -> `.spec.package`, `tag` -> `.status.tag`,
    `last_updated` -> `.status.conditions[?(@.type == 'Ready')].lastTransitionTime`
    (column type `date`, format `date-time`; the other six columns are type `string`),
    `stage` -> `.status.conditions[-1:].type`,
    `errors` -> `.status.conditions[?(@.status == 'False')].message`.
  Wire keys are fixed: the spec keys are `jukebox`, `category`, `package`, `initFrom`,
    `options`; @InitFrom serializes camelCase keys `secretName`, `subPath`, `snapshot`,
    `version`; the status struct carries no serde rename attribute so the status keys are
    verbatim `conditions`, `tag`, `digest`, `tfstate`, `rhaistate`, `befores`, `vitals`,
    `scalables`, `others`, `posts`, `crds`, `services`; @ApplicationCondition serializes
    camelCase keys `lastTransitionTime`, `message`, `type` (fixed by the @serde rename on
    @ApplicationCondition::condition_type), `status`, `generation`; @ConditionsType and
    @ConditionsStatus serialize as bare variant strings.
  @ConditionsType declares exactly fifteen variants serialized as their names: `Ready`
    (@Default), `Installed`, `Backuped`, `Restored`, `AgentStarted`, `CrdApplied`,
    `TofuInstalled`, `BeforeApplied`, `VitalApplied`, `ScalableApplied`, `InitFrom`,
    `ScheduleBackup`, `OtherApplied`, `RhaiApplied`, `PostApplied`; macro-attached constructors
    and setters write all of them except `Backuped` and `Restored`.
  @ServiceInstance::have_child answers `true` exactly when a status is present and at least one
    probe succeeds: `rhaistate` is `@Some` or `tfstate` is `@Some` regardless of content, or
    `befores`, `vitals`, `others`, `scalables`, `posts` or `crds` (in that order) is `@Some` and
    non-empty; probes short-circuit.
  @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names owns a process-wide cache: a function-local
    `static CACHE` @std::sync::LazyLock wrapping a @crate::TtlCache<@Vec<@String>> with a `30`
    second freshness window; a hit serves the cloned key list without building a client or
    touching the API server.
  On a miss the refresh performs one cluster-wide list (@kube::api::Api::all plus
    @kube::api::ListParams::default, every namespace) bounded by a separate `30` second
    @tokio::time::timeout literal, then flattens the @crate::Published `key` of every listed
    instance's `status.services` (@ServiceInstance::get_services defaults to empty), sorts the
    whole list lexicographically keeping duplicates, and on success caches and returns that
    sorted vector; on any failure the slot keeps its previous content and the next miss retries
    the full list (./ttl_cache.sdd).
  @ServiceInstance::rhai_list_services_names drives the async listing through
    @tokio::task::block_in_place combined with @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on, so it must
    run on a multi-thread runtime (@tokio::task::block_in_place panics on a current-thread
    runtime) and converts any failure through @crate::rhai_err into a string-carrying
    @rhai::EvalAltResult, losing the @crate::Error variant.
  @service_rhai_register registers the type under the script name `ServiceInstance` and wires
    exactly the script-visible surface mapped in `Exposes` — no other registration happens in
    this file; every mutator behind that surface, and the merge-patch/condition-rebuild semantics
    it triggers, behave as frozen in ./instance_macros.sdd.

Depends on:
  @impl_condition_common!, @impl_condition_children! and @impl_condition_crds! in
    ./instance_macros.rs — stamp @ApplicationCondition::new and supply the preset constructors
    for every stage this file's status enum names: ready/installed/agent/missing/tofu/rhai
    presets, the ten children-stage constructors plus @init_ko, @init_version_ko and
    @schedule_ko used by the befores expansion, and @crd_ok/@crd_ko; the expansion contract is
    ./instance_macros.sdd.
  @impl_instance_common!(ServiceInstance, "ServiceInstance") in ./instance_macros.rs — attach
    the status merge-patch (@ServiceInstance::patch_status, embedding the call-site kind literal
    `ServiceInstance`), the event recorder (@ServiceInstance::send_event), the private
    condition-rebuild helpers, and the shared lookup, options-digest, tfstate/rhaistate,
    agent/missing, tofu/rhai and metadata/spec/status Rhai surface that @service_rhai_register
    republishes; its @rhai_set_status_ready delegates to the @ServiceInstance::set_status_ready
    supplied by befores expansion.
  @impl_instance_befores!(ServiceInstance) in ./instance_macros.rs — attach
    @ServiceInstance::set_status_ready (the ready close the common macro's bridge compiles —
    the coupling recorded in ./instance_macros.sdd — is satisfied only by this expansion), the
    five children-stage success/failure setters, the init and schedule-backup failure setters,
    @ServiceInstance::set_services, and the synchronous @ServiceInstance::get_services read this
    file's cluster listing runs over every instance.
  @impl_instance_crds!(ServiceInstance) in ./instance_macros.rs — attach the CRD-stage setters
    and their Rhai wrappers, completing the stage @ConditionsType::CrdApplied names.
  @crate::TtlCache in ./ttl_cache.rs — the single-slot cache instance (window, coalescing and
    failure semantics owned by ./ttl_cache.sdd).
  @crate::context::get_client_async in ./context.rs — the shared @kube::Client for the
    cluster-wide list, fetched at refresh time only (cache hits build no client); it panics
    upstream when no client can be built.
  @crate::Published and @crate::Children in ./lib.rs — the published-service records flattened
    by the cluster listing and the child object records stored in the status lists.
  @crate::Error, @crate::Result, @crate::RhaiRes and @crate::rhai_err in ./lib.rs — the error
    contract propagated by the async listing and flattened to strings at the Rhai bridge.
  @kube::CustomResource, @kube::Resource, @kube::ResourceExt — the derive generating
    @ServiceInstance and the metadata/object-ref plumbing behind the macro-owned patching and
    event recording.
  @kube::api::Api and @kube::api::ListParams — the cluster-wide instance listing.
  @tokio::time::timeout, @tokio::task::block_in_place and @tokio::runtime::Handle — the call
    deadline on the listing and the sync-to-async bridge under the Rhai bridge.
  @rhai::Engine — the engine this file registers the bridge onto.

Exposes:
  @InitFrom — restore-request record with public fields @InitFrom::secret_name
    (`@Option<@String>`, wire `secretName`), @InitFrom::sub_path (`@Option<@String>`, wire
    `subPath`), @InitFrom::snapshot (`@String`, wire `snapshot`, the only required field) and
    @InitFrom::version (`@Option<@String>`, wire `version`); derives @Serialize, @Deserialize,
    @Eq, @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema. The doc comments declare defaults
    (`backup-settings` secret, `<namespace-name>/<app-slug>` path) that no code in this file
    applies.
  @ServiceInstanceSpec — CRD spec struct with public fields @ServiceInstanceSpec::jukebox,
    @ServiceInstanceSpec::category, @ServiceInstanceSpec::package,
    @ServiceInstanceSpec::init_from (`@Option<@InitFrom>`) and
    @ServiceInstanceSpec::options (`@Option<@serde_json::Map<@String, @serde_json::Value>>`);
    derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema via the
    @kube::CustomResource derive.
  @ServiceInstance — resource root generated by the @kube::CustomResource derive over
    @ServiceInstanceSpec, with fields `spec` (@ServiceInstanceSpec) and `status`
    (`@Option<@ServiceInstanceStatus>`).
  @ConditionsType — install-stage enum, the fifteen variants listed under `Must`, serialized as
    bare strings; derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Eq, @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug,
    @JsonSchema and @Default selecting `Ready`.
  @ConditionsStatus — enum `True` or `False`, serialized as those strings, with @Default
    selecting `True`; derives @Eq and @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema.
  @ApplicationCondition — one recorded condition with public fields
    @ApplicationCondition::last_transition_time (`@Option<@chrono::DateTime<@chrono::Utc>>`),
    @ApplicationCondition::message, @ApplicationCondition::condition_type,
    @ApplicationCondition::status and @ApplicationCondition::generation (`@i64`); derives
    @Eq and @PartialEq, compared field-by-field by the macro-owned dedup gate.
  Constructors attached to @ApplicationCondition by @impl_condition_common!:
    @ApplicationCondition::new,
    @ApplicationCondition::ready_ok, @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::installed_ok, @ApplicationCondition::installed_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::agent_started, @ApplicationCondition::missing_package,
    @ApplicationCondition::missing_box, @ApplicationCondition::missing_requirement,
    @ApplicationCondition::tofu_ok, @ApplicationCondition::tofu_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::rhai_ok, @ApplicationCondition::rhai_ko.
  Constructors attached by @impl_condition_children!: @ApplicationCondition::before_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::before_ko, @ApplicationCondition::vital_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::vital_ko, @ApplicationCondition::scalable_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::scalable_ko, @ApplicationCondition::other_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::other_ko, @ApplicationCondition::post_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::post_ko, @ApplicationCondition::init_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::init_version_ko, @ApplicationCondition::schedule_ko.
  Constructors attached by @impl_condition_crds!: @ApplicationCondition::crd_ok and
    @ApplicationCondition::crd_ko for @ConditionsType::CrdApplied.
  @ServiceInstanceStatus — status struct with public fields @ServiceInstanceStatus::conditions,
    @ServiceInstanceStatus::tag, @ServiceInstanceStatus::digest, @ServiceInstanceStatus::tfstate,
    @ServiceInstanceStatus::rhaistate, @ServiceInstanceStatus::befores,
    @ServiceInstanceStatus::vitals, @ServiceInstanceStatus::scalables,
    @ServiceInstanceStatus::others, @ServiceInstanceStatus::posts (each
    `@Option<@Vec<@crate::Children>>`), @ServiceInstanceStatus::crds (`@Option<@Vec<@String>>`)
    and @ServiceInstanceStatus::services (`@Option<@Vec<@crate::Published>>`); derives
    @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema.
  @ServiceInstance::have_child — child-state probe.
  @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names — cached cluster-wide published-key index.
  @ServiceInstance::rhai_list_services_names — synchronous Rhai bridge over the index.
  Methods attached by @impl_instance_common!: async @ServiceInstance::get, @ServiceInstance::list,
    @ServiceInstance::get_options_digest, @ServiceInstance::get_tfstate,
    @ServiceInstance::get_rhaistate, @ServiceInstance::set_tfstate,
