Accepts:
  Install coordinates as free-form strings in @ServiceInstanceSpec::jukebox,
    @ServiceInstanceSpec::category and @ServiceInstanceSpec::package,
    @ServiceInstanceSpec::options as any JSON object map or @None, and
    @ServiceInstanceSpec::init_from as any @InitFrom record or @None — this file never
    interprets `options` contents and never reads an @InitFrom field.
  @service_rhai_register takes a borrowed @rhai::Engine to decorate.
  The other in-file entry points take no arguments: @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names
    and @ServiceInstance::rhai_list_services_names are static, and @ServiceInstance::have_child
    takes only `&self`.

Returns:
  @ServiceInstance::have_child returns a `@bool` per the probe rules under `Must`.
  @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names returns @crate::Result<@Vec<@String>>: the merged,
    sorted, duplicates-kept list of every cached instance's published `key` values.
  @ServiceInstance::rhai_list_services_names returns @crate::RhaiRes<@Vec<@String>> wrapping
    the same vector.
  @service_rhai_register returns nothing.
  Returns of the macro-attached lookups, mutators and bridges follow ./instance_macros.sdd.

Raises:
  @crate::Error::Other with message `E_LIST_SERVICES_TIMEOUT: get_all_services_names exceeded 30s`
    when the cluster list does not resolve within its `30` second budget.
  @crate::Error::KubeError when the @kube listing call itself fails.
  On a refresh only, the upstream panic of @crate::context::get_client_async when no
    @kube::Client can be built; a cache hit never builds a client.
  @ServiceInstance::rhai_list_services_names flattens any @crate::Error through
    @crate::rhai_err into an @rhai::EvalAltResult message, and panics via
    @tokio::task::block_in_place on a current-thread @tokio runtime.
  Missing `snapshot` or a non-map `options` fails @ServiceInstanceSpec deserialization as a
    serde error before any method runs.
  Errors of the macro-attached mutators follow ./instance_macros.sdd.

Handles:
  Cluster list slower than `30` seconds — the timeout branch yields
    @crate::Error::Other in place of the @kube::Error mapping.
  @ServiceInstance with no status, or with `services` absent — contributes no key to the
    index (@ServiceInstance::get_services defaults to empty).
  The same `key` published by several instances — kept once per publisher; there is no dedup
    step after the sort.
  Fresh cache slot — clone served without any client or API call; concurrent misses coalesce
    to one refresh (./ttl_cache.sdd).
  Failed refresh — slot keeps its previous content, next call retries the full list.
  Generation-absent stamping, absent-status rebuild, surviving-`Ready` detection and
    event-publish failures during macro-attached mutators are owned by the expansions per
    ./instance_macros.sdd.

Tasks:
  [ ] No in-file @tests module exists, so none of the Scenarios below has a mapping test yet;
      cover them from these Scenario blocks under the project TTD rule when test work starts.
  [?] @ConditionsType::Backuped and @ConditionsType::Restored are written by no constructor,
      setter or event in the crate — wire-visible stage values the install flow can never
      produce. Decide later whether a backup flow will write them or they retire.
  [?] @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names keeps duplicate `key` values across instances
      (sort plus collect, no dedup). Decide later whether the index must be unique.
  [?] The index cache is a function-local @std::sync::LazyLock with lazy expiry only and no
      invalidation hook: a created, edited or deleted instance changes the visible index only
      after up to `30` seconds. Decide later whether an invalidation path is needed.
  [?] The cache window and the cluster-call timeout are two distinct `30` second literals that
      happen to be equal. Decide later whether they share one configuration point.
  [?] `list_service_instance` (@ServiceInstance::rhai_list, namespaced) and
      `list_services_names` (cluster-scoped @kube::api::Api::all) differ in namespace scope, so
      the latter requires cluster-wide read RBAC. Confirm the asymmetry is intended.
  [?] @InitFrom is a near-verbatim parallel copy of the @InitFrom in ./instancetenant.rs, and
      its doc-declared defaults (`backup-settings`, `<namespace-name>/<app-slug>`) are applied
      nowhere in this crate. Decide later whether the structs unify and where the defaults
      take effect.
  [?] @ServiceInstance::have_child is asymmetric: `tfstate`/`rhaistate` as @Some of the empty
      string count as a child, while @Some of an empty list in `befores`/`vitals`/`others`/
      `scalables`/`posts`/`crds` does not. Same finding as ./instancesystem.sdd; confirm.
  [?] Doc-comment drift: @ServiceInstanceSpec documents `Describe a source of vynil packages
      jukebox` (copied from the `JukeBox` model), the `# Errors` block of
      @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names omits the @crate::Error::Other timeout branch it
      raises before the @kube::Error one, and @InitFrom::version mixes French into the English
      docs. Rewrite wordings later.
  [?] @std::default::Default derives on @ConditionsType and @ConditionsStatus have no
      detectable use repo-wide. Decide later whether they stay.
  [?] @ServiceInstance::rhai_list_services_names joins the block_in_place bridge population:
      panics on a current-thread runtime and flattens @crate::Error to a string. The central
      multi-thread runtime decision is tracked in ./instance_macros.sdd and
      ./instancesystem.sdd; resolve once there.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing in-file test and `cargo test -p common` is green.

Scenario: Child-state probe
  Given a @ServiceInstance with no status at all, @ServiceInstance::have_child answers `false`
  But when only `rhaistate` or only `tfstate` is `@Some`, even the empty string, it answers
    `true`
  And when all six children lists are `@Some` of empty lists and no state is stored, it
    answers `false`
  And when only `crds` is `@Some` of one entry, it answers `true`
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet; see the open task above.

Scenario: Published-key index merges, sorts and keeps duplicates
  Given an empty cache and a cluster holding instances that publish keys `db.example` and
    `app.example`, one that publishes `db.example`, and one with no status at all
  When @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names is awaited
  Then the `@Ok` list is `app.example`, `db.example`, `db.example` in sort order
  And exactly one @kube listing is issued cluster-wide with @kube::api::ListParams::default
  And that sorted vector is what the `30` second cache window stores

Scenario: Fresh window absorbs the re-fetch
  Given one completed successful refresh within the `30` second window
  When @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names is awaited again
  Then the call returns the cloned cached list without a
    @crate::context::get_client_async fetch or any @kube call (./ttl_cache.sdd)

Scenario: Listing timeout names its error and caches nothing
  Given a @kube cluster listing that has not resolved within `30` seconds
  When @ServiceInstance::get_all_services_names is awaited
  Then the call returns @crate::Error::Other carrying
    `E_LIST_SERVICES_TIMEOUT: get_all_services_names exceeded 30s`
  And the cache slot keeps whatever it held before, so the next call re-runs the listing

Scenario: Script listing flattens a cluster failure
  Given a cluster listing failing with a @crate::Error::KubeError (or the timeout error)
  When a package script calls the registered `list_services_names` and
    @ServiceInstance::rhai_list_services_names runs
  Then the script receives an @rhai::EvalAltResult whose message is the flattened
    @crate::Error display text, the typed variant lost (./instance_macros.sdd bridge shape)

Scenario: initFrom wire shape requires a snapshot
  Given a `spec.initFrom` carrying `secretName` `backup-settings`, `subPath` `ns/app` and
    `snapshot` `abc123`
  When the @ServiceInstanceSpec deserializes, the fields land on @InitFrom with `version`
    @None
  But when `snapshot` is absent, deserialization fails as serde missing-field on the required
    @String, leaving no usable spec
